-- EU: Code of Practice on Transparency of AI-Generated Content (final, 10 June 2026),
-- Section 1, Measure 1.1 (machine-readable marking techniques), Sub-measures 1.1.1
-- and 1.1.2.
--
-- A VOLUNTARY code. It binds only providers that adhere to it. The Commission and the
-- AI Board have confirmed it is "an adequate voluntary tool" under Article 50(7) as
-- replaced by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744; adherence is the route this encoding
-- recognises for showing that a marking meets Article 50(2). It does not decide
-- whether any OTHER marking meets Article 50(2).
--
-- Source: source/eu-code-of-practice-transparency-2026-06-10.pdf, pages 8-9.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`

§ `Sub-measure 1.1.1 -- digitally signed metadata`

-- "If content is generated, manipulated or exported in a data format that supports
-- attaching metadata (e.g., an audio, image, video, or containerised text),
-- Signatories will record information in the metadata on whether the content is
-- AI-generated or manipulated. All recorded information will be digitally signed and
-- time-stamped (on systems where time information is available) in a secure and
-- tamper-evident manner."
-- A C2PA manifest records whether content is AI-generated or manipulated through its
-- digital source type, or its AI Disclosure assertion (C2PA 2.4, s.18.28).
GIVEN m IS A `C2PA manifest`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it records whether the content is AI-generated or manipulated` m IF
        elem `trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
    OR  elem `composite with trained algorithmic media` (m's `the source types it declares`)
    OR  m's `it carries an AI disclosure assertion`

-- "time-stamped (on systems where time information is available)": whether time
-- information was available on the generating system is not a fact this encoding
-- holds, so a manifest that records no time cannot be scored either way.
@ref Code of Practice, Sub-measure 1.1.1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`whether time information was available on the generating system is not modelled` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether time information was available on the generating system is not modelled"

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.1` content MEANS
    CONSIDER content's `the C2PA manifest it carries`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN
        IF      m's `its signature validates`
            AND `it records whether the content is AI-generated or manipulated` m
        THEN IF   m's `the time it records` EQUALS ""
             THEN `whether time information was available on the generating system is not modelled`
             ELSE TRUE
        ELSE FALSE

§ `Sub-measure 1.1.2 -- imperceptible watermarking`

-- "Signatories will ensure that AI-generated or manipulated content is marked with an
-- imperceptible watermark, with the exception of very short text."
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.2` content IF
    content's `it carries an imperceptible watermark`

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Sub-measure 1.1.2 excepts it as very short text` content IF
        `it is free-form text only` content
    AND content's `it is very short text`

GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is free-form text only` content IF
    all (GIVEN k YIELD k EQUALS `free-form text`) (content's `the kinds it contains`)
    AND NOT null (content's `the kinds it contains`)

§ `Measure 1.1 -- how many layers`

-- "Signatories will implement a multi-layered marking approach to ensure that the
-- outputs of their generative AI systems are marked with at least two layers of
-- machine-readable marking, as specified in Sub-measures 1.1.1 and 1.1.2 below."
-- Two single-layer cases follow:
--   (a) "a single layer of marking will be considered sufficient in specific cases
--       where a generative AI system is embedded in physical products capable of
--       generating synthetic outputs in a technically controlled and closed
--       environment mainly instructive in nature ... to the extent effective
--       technical measures are embedded in the product to prevent the output from
--       leaving the environment of the product";
--   (b) "given that free-form text cannot transport metadata, a single-layer of
--       marking as described in Sub-measure 1.1.2 is considered sufficient".
-- Very short free-form text is excepted from 1.1.2 and cannot carry 1.1.1, so on the
-- literal text Measure 1.1 asks nothing of it. NOTES fork F4.
@ref Code of Practice, Measure 1.1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provider does not adhere to the Code of Practice, and whether its marking meets Article 50(2) is an assessment this encoding does not make` MEANS
    REFUSE "the provider does not adhere to the Code of Practice, and whether its marking meets Article 50(2) is an assessment this encoding does not make"

@ref Code of Practice, Measure 1.1, Sub-measures 1.1.1 and 1.1.2
GIVEN content IS A `piece of content`, provider IS A `the provider of the AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the marking meets Measure 1.1 of the Code of Practice` content provider MEANS
    IF NOT provider's `it adheres to Section 1 of the EU Code of Practice`
    THEN `the provider does not adhere to the Code of Practice, and whether its marking meets Article 50(2) is an assessment this encoding does not make`
    ELSE BRANCH
            IF `Sub-measure 1.1.2 excepts it as very short text` content
                THEN TRUE
            IF `it is free-form text only` content
                THEN `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.2` content
            IF content's `it stays inside a closed physical product`
                THEN    `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.2` content
                     OR `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.1` content
            OTHERWISE   `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.1` content
                    AND `the content carries the layer in Sub-measure 1.1.2` content
